<title>UK: Smith &amp; Nephew chairman to retire in June.</title>
<headline>Smith &amp; Nephew chairman to retire in June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Healthcare firm Smith &amp; Nephew said its chairman Eric Kinder will be retiring at the end of the June to be succeeded by current chief executive John Robinson.</p>
<p>Deputy chief executive Chris O'Donnell will replace Robinson, Smith &amp; Nephew said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
